cks for an explicit meta‑schema IRI and loads it.'}]}, {'group': 'getSchema(SchemaLocation) - caching behavior', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'classpath:/schemas/cached-schema.json'}], 'expected': 'The first and second calls to getSchema with the same SchemaLocation return the identical JsonSchema instance (reference equality), demonstrating that the factory caches loaded schemas.', 'description': 'Verifies that the factory does not reload a schema that has already been parsed and cached, which is important for performance and for preserving identity semantics across the application.'}]}, {'group': 'getSchema(SchemaLocation) - HTTP URI handling', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'http://localhost:8080/remote-schema.json'}], 'expected': 'Returns a non‑null JsonSchema instance loaded from the HTTP resource. The meta‑schema version matches the $schema keyword present in the remote file.', 'description': 'Ensures that the factory can resolve a SchemaLocation that uses the HTTP scheme, fetch the content over the network, and parse it correctly.'}]}, {'group': 'getSchema(SchemaLocation) - YAML format support', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'classpath:/schemas/yaml-schema.yaml'}], 'expected': 'Returns a non‑null JsonSchema instance whose structure matches the YAML definition. No exception is thrown, confirming that the factory auto‑detects YAML input format.', 'description': 'Tests that a schema stored in YAML (instead of JSON) is correctly read by the factory via the default YamlMapper.'}]}, {'group': 'getSchema(SchemaLocation) - unknown $schema version fallback', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'classpath:/schemas/unknown-meta-schema.json'}], 'expected': "Returns a JsonSchema instance using the library's default meta‑schema (latest supported draft). No exception is thrown even though the $schema IRI is not recognized.", 'description': 'Validates that when a schema declares an unknown or unsupported $schema IRI, the factory falls back to the default meta‑schema rather than failing outright.'}]}, {'group': 'getSchema(SchemaLocation) - cyclic $ref detection', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'classpath:/schemas/cyclic-schema.json'}], 'expected': 'Throws a JsonSchemaException (or a subclass) with a message indicating a cyclic $ref resolution was detected.', 'description': "Provides a schema where definition A $ref's B and B $ref's A. The test confirms that the loader detects the cycle and aborts with a clear exception rather than entering infinite recursion."}]}, {'group': 'getSchema(SchemaLocation) - relative $ref with $id resolution', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'classpath:/schemas/relative-ref-schema.json'}], 'expected': 'Returns a JsonSchema where the relative $ref is correctly resolved against the base URI defined by the $id keyword in the same document.', 'description': 'Ensures that the factory respects the $id base URI for relative reference resolution, a subtle but required part of the JSON‑Schema spec.'}]}, {'group': 'getSchema(SchemaLocation) - custom SchemaLoader via builder', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'classpath:/schemas/custom-loader-schema.json'}], 'expected': 'The returned JsonSchema originates from the custom SchemaLoader supplied to the factory builder (e.g., a mock loader that returns a predefined JsonNode). The test asserts that the loader’s `loadSchema` method was invoked.', 'description': 'Demonstrates that a user‑provided SchemaLoader can override the default loading mechanism, allowing injection of mocked or pre‑processed schemas.'}]}, {'group': 'getSchema(SchemaLocation) - legacy draft‑04 meta‑schema handling', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'schemaUri', 'value': 'classpath:/schemas/draft04-schema.json'}], 'expected': 'Returns a JsonSchema whose meta‑schema version is DraftV4 (the library’s representation of draft‑04). The